---
import SectionLink from './SectionLink.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="fansociety">
	<div class="wrap">
		<span class="numeral" aria-hidden="true">05</span>

		<p class="eyebrow">FanSociety</p>
		<h2>Crowdfunding patronage for musicians and fans</h2>

		<div class="intro">
			<p class="lede">
				Though accessible, subscriptions are not durable.
				We landed on a simple solution, a one time donation provides capital to artists and can also timestamp when a fan discovered an artist.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="split">
			<article class="side">
				<div class="side-head">
					<h3>For you</h3>
					<span class="tag">artist</span>
				</div>
				<ul>
					<li>An additional source of income through crowdfunding while avoiding subscription fatigue.</li>
					<li>Grant early releases, bonus tracks, or free streaming to any generation you choose — per album, or per track.</li>
					<li>Integrated with Station on day one; easy to manage in your self hosted artist dashboard.</li>
					<li>Identify fans based on when they join your community, with the flexibility to give back to them in meaningful ways.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="side">
				<div class="side-head">
					<h3>For them</h3>
					<span class="tag">fan</span>
				</div>
				<ul>
					<li>Digital proof that they were an early fan, durable social currency.</li>
					<li>Get special access granted by artists; digital products, physical products, and event tickets.</li>
					<li>Support artists directly with a provable minimally extractive payments system.</li>
					<li>Stronger tie to the artist, doesn't depend on success of a single business to be durable and long lasting.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</div>

		<p class="margin-note">
			The social contract between a fan and an artist already exists. FanSociety just records it
			somewhere neither party can edit later.
		</p>

		<SectionLink slug="fansociety" />
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.intro {
		margin: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
	}

	.intro p + p {
		margin-top: 1.1rem;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
	}

	.intro strong {
		color: var(--mint);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.split {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1px;
		background: var(--rule);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.side {
		background: var(--black);
		padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
	}

	.side-head {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-bottom: 1.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mint-rule);
	}

	h3 {
		color: var(--mint);
	}

	.tag {
		font-size: 0.6rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--gray-dim);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
		transform: rotate(1deg);
	}

	ul {
		list-style: none;
	}

	li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.4rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
	}

	li + li {
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
	}

	li::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		top: 0.62em;
		width: 0.6rem;
		height: 1px;
		background: var(--mint);
	}
</style>
